<title>USA: Ford doubles Taurus rebates to $1,000 - WSJ.</title>
<headline>Ford doubles Taurus rebates to $1,000 - WSJ.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ford Motor Co has doubled the rebate on its 1997 Taurus sedan to $1,000, with less than two weeks to go before sales are tallied for the year, The Wall Street Journal reported Thursday.</p>
<p>Through November Taurus sales were 9,700 ahead of rival Honda Accord, the story says.</p>
<p>But sales of 1997 models are already lagging behind the Accord, the report said.</p>
</text>
